2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/99561793/knudt-o.-teig
2 CONT
2 CONT Knudt O. Teig BIRTH	7 Sep 1827 Sauda kommune, Rogaland fylke, Norway DEATH	29 Jun 1909 (aged 81) Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Roland Cemetery Howard Township, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Ole Teig and Gunhild Berkeland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roland Record  1 July 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT Octogenarian Passes to Rest
2 CONT
2 CONT Aged Resident of Roland Dies After Several Months Sickness, Was Eighty-Two Years Old, Leaves Many Relatives
2 CONT
2 CONT Knudt O. Teig died Tuesday morning from several months sickness at the home of his brother, Paul O. Teig and family at this place. The deceased was born in Sovde, near Stavanger, September 7, 1827 and was 81 years, 9 months and 22
2 CONC  days old at the time of his death. He was married in Norway to Miss Martha Oldsdatter Hereim in 1846, who died March 27, 1895 and is buried at this place. Seven children are left to mourn the loss of a kind father. They are Ole T
2 CONC eig, of Lakefield, Minn., Ole K. Teig, of Windom, Minn., K. K. Teig, of this place; Mrs. Annie Durby, of McCallsburg; Martin K. Teig, of Seattle, Wash.; Knudt K. Teig, of Alaska and Mrs. Gusta Olson, of Seattle, Wash. Besides his 
2 CONC children, he leaves a sister, Mrs. Martha Teig, in Norway; and two brothers, Paul O. Teig, of this place, and John Teig, of Story City, and numerous other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1881, he came to this country with his wife and has since lived in and near Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was held from Bergen Church, of which he was an active member, on Wednesday afternoon, Rev. G. Smedal officiating. A very large number of people attended the funeral services, the church being filled to the utmost. Int
2 CONC erment took place in the Roland cemetery. The sorrowing families are extended the sincere sympathy of their numerous friends in the hour of their bereavement.
2 CONT
2 CONT [NOTE - the obituary for Martin Langland also appears in the 1 July 1909 Roland Record, and it indicates that the services for Martin Langland and Knudt Teig were perhaps concurrent]
