1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.trftimes.com/news/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=9446:harlan-garfve-75&catid=6:death-notices&Itemid=3
2 CONT
2 CONT Newfolden - Harlan Garfve, 75, died on Sunday, August 21, 2011 at Oakland Park Communities in Thief River Falls.
2 CONT      Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. on Thursday, Aug. 25 at Westaker Free Lutheran Church in Newfolden, with Pastor Phil Rokke officiating. Interment will follow at Oak Grove Cemetery in Newfolden.
2 CONT      Visitation will be held from 5 to 8 p.m., with 7 p.m. prayer service on Wednesday, Aug. 24,  at Johnson Funeral Service in Thief River Falls. Visitation will also be held from 1 to 2 p.m. on Thursday at the church.
2 CONT      Harlan Roger Garfve was born April 26, 1936 on the family farm near Newfolden, the youngest son of nine children born to Hjalmer and Bella (Tunheim) Garfve.  He was baptized into the Lutheran faith at Westaker Free Lutheran C
2 CONC hurch.  He attended school in Newfolden.
2 CONT      Harlan went to California in 1956 and worked road construction for a couple of years. He then returned to live in Newfolden, where he continued to work road construction.  Harlan could run all of the machinery but operating t
2 CONC he turnapole (scraper) was his favorite. He loved his work.  During the winter months, Harlan would cut wood and had many customers in the Newfolden area. He would cut over 100 cord of wood in the winter time.
2 CONT      In the late 1950s, Harlan was married to Delores Gustafson for about five years. In 1964, he married Arlette Brekkestrand in Colorado and to this union six children were born, Sharon, Angie, Sharlene, Duke, Roger and Tina.
2 CONT      On Dec. 18, 1992, Harlan was united in marriage to Sigrid B. Ruddy in Sisseton, S.D. They continued to make their home in Newfolden.
2 CONT      Harlan enjoyed hunting, fishing, collecting scrap iron, cutting wood, playing pull tabs, listening to music, especially Johnny Cash and attending auction sales. He especially enjoyed spending time with his family and the four
2 CONC th of July holiday.
2 CONT      Harlan was a 26-year vested member of the Operating Engineers Local 49 Union.
2 CONT      Survivors include his loving wife of 18 years, Sigrid of Newfolden;  five children, Angie (Pete) Lefrooth of Strandquist, Sharlene Tostrup of Viking, Duke (Wendy) Garfve of Warren, Roger Garfve of Newfolden, and Tina Garfve o
2 CONC f Middle River; daughter-in-law, Bobbi Jo Garfve of Halma; step-children, Judith Ruddy of Coon Rapids, Nancy Ruddy of Newfolden, Michael (Susan) Ruddy of Apple Valley, Carrie (Robert) Schmidt of North Branch, Randy (Marty) Ruddy o
2 CONC f Lino Lakes; 17 grandchildren; eight step-grandchildren; one great-granddaughter; 10 step great-grandchildren;  two sisters, Sandra Larson of Goodridge and Barbara (Ronnie) Benke of Newfolden; brother-in-law, Carvel Gillund of Th
2 CONC ief River Falls; sister-in-law, Joan Garfve of Alpina, S.D.; and many nieces, nephews, relatives and friends.
2 CONT      He was preceded in death by daughter, Sharon Torgerson; granddaughter, Morgan McAnnany; parents; sisters, Helen, Rosemary, Phyllis, Mabel and Ruby; and brother, Maynard.    A00003B2011AG24
2 CONT
