1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/201024974/beverly-irma-lindstrom
2 CONT
2 CONT Beverly Irma Berggren Lindstrom
2 CONT BIRTH	13 Feb 1939
2 CONT Marshall County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT DEATH	4 Jul 2019 (aged 80)
2 CONT Fargo, Cass County, North Dakota, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Wanger Baptist Cemetery
2 CONT Marshall County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Beverly Irma (Berggren) Lindstrom was born to Yngve and Elsie Berggren on February 13, 1939, at the family farm near Strandquist Minnesota. She was promoted to heaven from hospice care at Rosewood on Broadway on July 4, 2019, with
2 CONC  family by her side.
2 CONT
2 CONT She graduated from Strandquist school in 1957 and cherished her school friends through her whole life. Beverly married Carroll Lindstrom of Argyle Minnesota on June 27, 1958 and to this union three sons were born: Randy, Calvin an
2 CONC d Alan. They lived on the Lindstrom farm until 2007 when they moved into Newfolden for three years before moving to live with Calvin near Duluth. After Carroll’s passage, Bev moved to Fargo along with Calvin and Kristi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bev enjoyed playing piano and organ at the Newfolden Evangelical Free and Alma Lutheran Churches, and at funerals. She was an avid crafter/recycler, quilter, and notable baker of wedding and graduation cakes. She worked in the ASC
2 CONC  office in Warren after high school and then in the school office in Strandquist. Beverly was a homemaker, babysitter, and piano teacher. After raising her family she became a Marshall County assessor for 15 years, custodian for t
2 CONC he Argyle Migrants School, and home care assistant for the county for a season. She was an active member of the Newfolden Evangelical Free Church for many years serving in various teaching, ministry, and treasury positions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beverly is survived by two brothers, Newell (Loretta) Berggren and Gene (Lana) Berggren; three sons, Randy (Diane) Lindstrom, Calvin (Kristi) Lindstrom of Fargo, and Alan (Janet) Lindstrom; 14 grandchildren and 17 great grandchild
2 CONC ren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, Carroll, her parents Yngve and Elsie Berggren, and an infant granddaughter, Rachel.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family will be handling services in Newfolden, Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation is scheduled for Monday, July 15 at 6:30 pm at the Evangelical Free Church of Newfolden, Minnesota, with a devotional service at 7:00pm. The Memorial Service will be held at 11:00 a.m. Tuesday, July 16, 2019, at the New
2 CONC folden Evangelical Free Church. Interment to follow at Wanger Baptist Cemetery, near Argyle, Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adapted from Boulger Funeral Home obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Yngve Berggren
2 CONT 1907–1979
2 CONT
2 CONT Elsie Pauline Tunheim Berggren
2 CONT 1910–1997
