1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/203401007/barbara-jeanne-bring
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Jeanne Hanson Bring
2 CONT BIRTH	6 Aug 1935
2 CONT Marshall County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT DEATH	23 Sep 2019 (aged 84)
2 CONT Pennington County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Bethania Cemetery
2 CONT Marsh Grove, Marshall County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Bring of Thief River Falls, MN, formerly of Newfolden, MN passed away peacefully with her family by her side, at the Thief River Care Center on Monday, September 23, 2019 at the age of 84.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service will be held on Friday, September 27, 2019 at 11:00 AM at Westaker Lutheran Church in Newfolden, MN with Pastor Wes Langaas officiating. Burial will be held at Bethania Cemetery, Newfolden, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held from 5:00 PM until 7:00 PM with a 7:00 PM Prayer Service on Thursday, September 26, 2019 at Johnson Funeral Service in Thief River Falls, MN. Visitation will also be held one hour prior to the service at th
2 CONC e church on Friday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Jeanne (Hanson) Bring was born on August 6, 1935 in Middle River, MN, the daughter of Hjalmer and Mildred (Kalishko) Hanson. She was baptized on January 9, 1936. Barbara attended school in Middle River and Gatzke.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her teens she worked at a nursing home in Middle River and also helped take care of her siblings. At the age of 18 she moved to St. Paul, MN, where she worked until she met her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 19, 1958 Barbara was united in marriage to Gordon Bring in Middle River. They made their home in Newfolden, MN, on the Bring family farm and raised four children: John, Roger, Karyl, and Karl. Together they raised dairy c
2 CONC attle and small grain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara also worked with the potato harvest, worked as a custodian at the Newfolden School and the Newfolden elevator. Throughout her lifetime she took care of many various family members. Barbara cared deeply for her family; they
2 CONC  meant the world to her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara was an active member of Bethania Lutheran Church, always willing to help in any capacity that was needed, whether it was mowing the church yard, serving in the kitchen, or cooking for events and baking for the bake sales. 
2 CONC Her angel food cakes were always sought after. When Bethania stopped having regular services, Barbara and Gordon continued attending and serving at Westaker Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara enjoyed sewing, quilting, knitting, embroidery, Artex painting, gardening, cooking, and baking. She was well known for her potato dumplings, beef stew with biscuits, chicken dumpling soup, and cinnamon rolls. Barbara loved
2 CONC  spending time with friends and family, visiting, playing cards and board games. She had a very competitive spirit – she was in it to win it!
2 CONT
2 CONT In her later years she and Gordon moved into Newfolden and became active in the senior citizen group where Barbara was known for her embroidered dishtowels that were sold at the Newfolden Community Center. In 2006 Barbara and Gord
2 CONC on were named Outstanding Senior Citizens and represented Newfolden at the Marshall County Fair.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the summer of 2018 Barbara and Gordon moved to assisted living at Valley Home in Thief River Falls.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara is survived by her husband, Gordon of Thief River Falls, MN; children, John (Betty) Bring of Thief River Falls, MN, Roger (Reta) Bring of Newfolden, MN, Karyl Grochowski of Donaldson, MN, and Karl (Lisa) Bring of Newfolden
2 CONC , MN; grandchildren, Sara Bring, Wendy (Joel) Robinette, Kaitlin Mock, Logan Bring, Mason Bring, Dustin Carpenter, Corey (Sheila) Grochowski, Jeremy Grochowski, Austin (Brooke) Grochowski, Kassidy Hultgren, Tory Bring, Tanya Bring
2 CONC , Hannah Peterson, Alexis Bring, and Luke Bring; 20 great-grandchildren; brothers, Hjalmer (Patty) Hanson of Middle River, MN and John Hanson of Centerville, MN; sister, Karyl (Tom) Cooper of St. Paul, MN; many nieces, nephews, co
2 CONC usins, relatives, and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents; and her sister, Margaret (Kermit) Strandberg.
2 CONT
