2 DATE 21 JUL 1919
1 OCCU @occu00029@
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Occupation Details
2 CONT
2 CONT Teodor 's occupation was Slagter-Butcher in 1900 census Sokndal .
2 CONT
2 CONT       General notes: b. in Resland, changed name to Olsen when he lived with Aunt at farm "Eia" after father died in a mining accident.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Lived in Sokndalsstrands, as per records received from Oslo archives
2 CONT
2 CONT       In 1865 census for Sokndal he was at the farm Eia. The census tells that Theodor was the foster child to Siri Tønnesdatter and Tobias Larsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT       In 1900 census he was in Sokndal.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Theodor Refsland Eia
2 CONT
2 CONT       Ekteskap Barn
2 CONT
2 CONT       - - Berthe Egeland 17 Apr 1900 - Adelaide Magdalena Eia
2 CONT
2 CONT       However, we have made some research, and in the local history book or “bygdebok” by Petrus Valand and Olav Heskestad: “Hetland skipreide i 450 år”, volume 1 (1971), we have found information on the farm Helleren in Heskestad
2 CONC  in Lund municipality (kommune), Rogaland county (fylke).
2 CONT
2 CONT       According to the “bygdebok” Ole Toresen Helleren was born on 12 December 1824, and he came from the farm Revsland. On 27 June 1853 he married the widow Anne Tønnesdatter Helleren, cf. the marriage rercord in parish register 
2 CONC for Lund/Heskestad (no 3) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20051212050275.jpg.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Anne Tønnesdatter’s first husband was Asbjørn Børildsen Helleren, and according to the “bygdebok” they married in Sokndal. They had three children: Børild, Tønnes and Lisabeth. Anne Tønnesdatter was born 11 June 1820 in Sokn
2 CONC dal (former: Sogndal), cf. (no 28) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20070625630649.jpg. Her parents were Tønnes Jakobsen and Anne Sofie Jonsdatter Hetleskog (former: Hetleskou).
2 CONT
2 CONT       We have found the birth and baptism record for Theodor Olsen Helleren from 1861 in the digitised parish register for Lund/Heskestad, cf. (no 5) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020356.jpg. Theodor Olsen had two 
2 CONC elder sisters, Ingeborg Tobine, born 1854 in Heskestad, cf. (no 7):
2 CONT
2 CONT       www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020325.jpg, and Alette Johanne, born 1856, cf. (no 2): www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020330.jpg. There were also two elder brothers called Theodor, born in 1857 a
2 CONC nd 1859, but they both died as very small.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Here is the death record for Ole Toresen Helleren from 1861, which tells that he was killed by a blasting shot (“Dræbt ved en Mineskud” – written in Danish), cf. digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=7
2 CONC 9&filnamn=gr11131854b&gardpostnr=161&personpostnr=162&merk=162#ovre and the digitised parish register (no 6) http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020587.jpg.
2 CONT
2 CONT       In 1865 census for Sokndal we have found Theodor Olsen on the farm Eia, cf.:  http://digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=65&filnamn=f61111&gardpostnr=485&personpostnr=2936&merk=2936#ovre. The census 
2 CONC tells that Theodor was the foster child to Siri Tønnesdatter and Tobias Larsen. Siri Tønnesdatter was 47 years old in 1865, and in the parish register for Sokndal we have found the birth and baptism record for Siri, born on 21 Jun
2 CONC e 1818, cf. www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20070625630633.jpg. Siri’s father was Tønnes Jakobsen Hetleskog. The mother’s patronymic is written Iversdatter, but we suggest that Siri is the sister to Anne Tønnesdatter, born 1
2 CONC 820, since the farm name “Hetleskou” is the same in the birth and baptism records.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Theodor Olsen married Berte Guri Pedersdatter in Heskestad in 1882, cf. (no 5) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020571.jpg. We have found the butcher (slakteren) Theodor Eia in the 1900 census for Sokndal, cf.: 
2 CONC digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=3&filnamn=f01107&gardpostnr=60&personpostnr=252&merk=252#ovre.
2 CONT
2 CONT       We enclose scanned copies of the “bygdebok” with information on the farms  Helleren and Revsland, including the ancestry of Ole Toresen / Torsen Helleren.  
2 CONT
2 CONT       Yours sincerely,
2 CONT
2 CONT       Grethe Flood, by authority
2 CONT
2 CONT       Archivist
2 CONT
2 CONT       However, we have made some research, and in the local history book or “bygdebok” by Petrus Valand and Olav Heskestad: “Hetland skipreide i 450 år”, volume 1 (1971), we have found information on the farm Helleren in Heskestad
2 CONC  in Lund municipality (kommune), Rogaland county (fylke).
2 CONT
2 CONT       According to the “bygdebok” Ole Toresen Helleren was born on 12 December 1824, and he came from the farm Revsland. On 27 June 1853 he married the widow Anne Tønnesdatter Helleren, cf. the marriage rercord in parish register 
2 CONC for Lund/Heskestad (no 3) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20051212050275.jpg.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Anne Tønnesdatter’s first husband was Asbjørn Børildsen Helleren, and according to the “bygdebok” they married in Sokndal. They had three children: Børild, Tønnes and Lisabeth. Anne Tønnesdatter was born 11 June 1820 in Sokn
2 CONC dal (former: Sogndal), cf. (no 28) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20070625630649.jpg. Her parents were Tønnes Jakobsen and Anne Sofie Jonsdatter Hetleskog (former: Hetleskou).
2 CONT
2 CONT       We have found the birth and baptism record for Theodor Olsen Helleren from 1861 in the digitised parish register for Lund/Heskestad, cf. (no 5) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020356.jpg. Theodor Olsen had two 
2 CONC elder sisters, Ingeborg Tobine, born 1854 in Heskestad, cf. (no 7):
2 CONT
2 CONT       www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020325.jpg, and Alette Johanne, born 1856, cf. (no 2): www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020330.jpg. There were also two elder brothers called Theodor, born in 1857 a
2 CONC nd 1859, but they both died as very small.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Here is the death record for Ole Toresen Helleren from 1861, which tells that he was killed by a blasting shot (“Dræbt ved en Mineskud” – written in Danish), cf. digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=7
2 CONC 9&filnamn=gr11131854b&gardpostnr=161&personpostnr=162&merk=162#ovre and the digitised parish register (no 6) http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020587.jpg.
2 CONT
2 CONT       In 1865 census for Sokndal we have found Theodor Olsen on the farm Eia, cf.:  http://digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=65&filnamn=f61111&gardpostnr=485&personpostnr=2936&merk=2936#ovre. The census 
2 CONC tells that Theodor was the foster child to Siri Tønnesdatter and Tobias Larsen. Siri Tønnesdatter was 47 years old in 1865, and in the parish register for Sokndal we have found the birth and baptism record for Siri, born on 21 Jun
2 CONC e 1818, cf. www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20070625630633.jpg. Siri’s father was Tønnes Jakobsen Hetleskog. The mother’s patronymic is written Iversdatter, but we suggest that Siri is the sister to Anne Tønnesdatter, born 1
2 CONC 820, since the farm name “Hetleskou” is the same in the birth and baptism records.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Theodor Olsen married Berte Guri Pedersdatter in Heskestad in 1882, cf. (no 5) www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061121020571.jpg. We have found the butcher (slakteren) Theodor Eia in the 1900 census for Sokndal, cf.: 
2 CONC digitalarkivet.uib.no/cgiwin/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=3&filnamn=f01107&gardpostnr=60&personpostnr=252&merk=252#ovre.
2 CONT
2 CONT       We enclose scanned copies of the “bygdebok” with information on the farms  Helleren and Revsland, including the ancestry of Ole Toresen / Torsen Helleren.  
2 CONT
2 CONT       Yours sincerely,
2 CONT
2 CONT       Grethe Flood, by authority
