1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Folketællinger: FT-1880 Vestergade matr.26, stuen/1.sal, Køge Købstad, Roskilde Amt, 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Viggo RITZAU (1873-1957), police chief, was a pioneering Danish Esperantist. Already in 1905 Ritzau became an Esperantist and participated in 1906 in the 2nd UK in Geneva as the only Dane. As a lawyer he served in the district chi
2 CONC ef's office in Ebeltoft from 1898-1905 and later until 1910 in the governor's office in Randers, in both places as a procurator. But during those years Ritzau did not officially take part in the work for Esperanto.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the years 1919-1943 Ritzau was a police chief in Køge, and since then he has been actively involved in the Esperanto movement as a co-founder of the local club, of which he is always a member, and in recent years he even leads 
2 CONC courses in the evening school.
