2 CONT Obituary source, The Roland Record, May 7, 1908
2 CONT "RESPECTED LADY LAID TO REST
2 CONT Mrs. A.B. Anderson Died Friday and Funeral is Held Tuesday From Bergen Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sad, yet not wholly unexpected, news reached here Friday evening that Mrs. Andrew B. Anderson, living nine miles southeast of here, had passed away, her ailment having been acute rheumatism with a weak heart. She has suffered 
2 CONC more or less for several years, but has been able to be around until a few weeks ago, when she was taken seriously sick, and death came to her relief on Friday evening, May 1, 1908.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Julia Thompson was a daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Oscar Thompson, of this place, and was born near Lisbon, Ill., June 2, 1865. The next year she came with her parents to Story County where she has since resided. She was married t
2 CONC o Andrew B. Anderson on March 20, 1884, to which union ten children were born, all of whom are at home. They are: Ove, Annie, Allia, Bertha, Oscar, Josie, Rosie, Amos, Clarence and Irwin. Besides these she leaves her parents, Mr. 
2 CONC and Mrs. Oscar Thompson, two brothers Abel and Oscar, of this place and three sisters, Mrs. John Halvorson, of Dallas, Wis., Henry Stoll, of near Fernald, and Mrs. John Nerem, of near Radcliffe and numerous other relatives and fri
2 CONC ends.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a quiet and home loving woman, who numbered her friends by her acquaintances and who will be greatly missed by her family to whom she was very much devoted.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was held Tuesday May 5, from Bergen church, Rev. Smedal officiating, afte which interment took place in the Roland cemetery. The church was filled with friends who wished to pay their last tribute to the dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Record extends to the bereaved ones its sincere sympathy in the hour of their sorrow."
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Julie, wife of A.B. Anderson
