2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/119591352/knut-paulson-teig
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Paulson Teig BIRTH	9 Dec 1874 Norway DEATH	9 Oct 1951 (aged 76) Des Moines, Polk County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Roland Cemetery Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary source, The Roland Record, October 18, 1951
2 CONT
2 CONT "LAST RITES FOR KNUT P. TEIG
2 CONT
2 CONT LIVED IN THE ROLAND COMMUNITY NEARLY ALL HIS LIFE
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut P. Teig was born December 9, 1874 in Sovde, Norway. His parents were Paul O. and Britta Teig, and with them he came to America May 31, 1880, at the age of five years, and they settled on a farm south of Roland. On November 10
2 CONC , 1889, he was confirmed in the Bergen Lutheran church by Rev. Claus Jacobson.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 31, 1903 he was united in marriage to Mary Grove at her parent's home in Roland, by Rev. J.N. Sandven. They bought a farm two miles east and one mile south of Roland where they established a home and lived for 43 years
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT After retiring from the farm they resided in Nevada for two years until they bought a home in Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT To this union seven children were born. Edward, a twin to Ellen, died in infancy. (The six living children are: Palmer of Osceola, Mons of Ellsworth, Hubert on the home farm, Virgnia (Mrs. Victor McKinney) of Colo, Kermit of West 
2 CONC Union, and Ellen (Mrs. Orris Osheim) of Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Teig was vitally interested in all agricultural, community and church organizations. He gave freely of his time to his many duties. He was a prominent member of the Story County Farm Bureau, of which he was president and count
2 CONC y 4-H committeeman for man years. His many public duties included being president of the Farmers Cooperative Creamery, secretary of the Farmers Cooperative Elevator, president of the Story County Cow Testing association, and an ac
2 CONC tive member of his church.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to farming, he and his sons operated a dairy in Roland for twenty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 24 of this year he entered Mercy hospital in Des Moines to prepare for surgery. His condition became steadily worse and he passed away Tuesday, October 9 at the age of 76 years and 10 months.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his passing he leaves to mourn his death, his widow, six children, and 10 grandchildren. He is also survived by two brothers and two sisters: Peter of Roland and Ben of Adel, Carrie (Mrs. Lars Haugen) of St. Paul, Minn., and Am
2 CONC anda (Mrs. C.J. Henryson) of Billings, Mont. all of whom were present at the funeral. His parents and several brothers and sisters preceded him in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Friday afternoon, October 12, with a prayer service at the home, where O.S. Boyd sang "In The Garden"; and at Bergen Lutheran church where O.S. Boyd and Don H. Boyd sang a duet, "Jesus Lover of My Soul,"
2 CONC  and Otto J. Hanson sang, "Den Store Hvide Flok." Rev. Allen E. Nelson officiated at the services. Mrs. Herbert Houser of Whitten, Mrs. Wm. Dailey of Ames, and Mrs. Overt I. Holland of Roland were in charge of the flowers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall bearers were nephews of the deceased: Boyd Teig of St. Paul, Minn., Carrol Teig of Des Moines, John McDonald of Des Moines, Harold McCord of Denison, James McCord of Storm Lake and Charles West of Oskaloosa. Burial was made i
2 CONC n the Roland cemetery.
2 CONT
