2 CONT After his wife died, Nils never remarried and raised his sons Nils and Knut alone.  In 1857 Nils Nilsen and his two sons came to America. They left from Drammen on the sailing ship "Familien".  It took five weeks to reach Quebec, 
2 CONC Canada.  From there they traveled to Stoughton, WI by canal boat and train  ( in a cattle car with wooden benches to sit on ).  From Stoughton they traveled by oxcart to Koshkonong, WI.  The first winter they lived in a kitchen, 1
2 CONC 2 feet square, that had been built in a haybarn attached to a horsebarn.  The next four years they lived in several places at Koshkonong.    In the Spring of 1862 they went to Norway Lake in Kandiohi County, MN, with the idea of g
2 CONC etting land.  They had come just in time for an Indian War and came back south to the home of Gunhild and Ole at Goodhue.  They spent the Winter there and Nils died the following summer.  The sons remained at Goodhue.
