1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT When Nils and his sons left for America, Barbo and her husband Halvor, took over South Veslegard.  But in 1860 they sold it and sometime during the 1860's they came to America. They came first to Gunhild's home in Goodhue and then
2 CONC  settled in Northern Iowa.  In 1878 or 1879 Halvor moved to Hatton, ND, but it is not known whether Barbro was still living at that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for BARBRO NILSEDATTER LILLEGARD:
2 CONT When Nils and his sons left for America, Barbro and Halvor took over South Veslegard. But in 1876 they sold it and came to America.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT Digitalarkivet Emigranter fra Oslo 1867-1930: On 28 Apr 1876, Barbro, husband Halvor, and sons Halvor and Knudt departed Oslo on the "Angelo" line - Betalt, destination - Albert Lea, Minnesota.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT They came first to Goodhue and then settled in northern Iowa.   In 1878, Halvor moved to Hatton, North Dakota, but it is not known whether Barbro was still living at that time.   Halvor died in Hatton in 1890.   The two oldest son
2 CONC s, Osten and Nils, became very well known as carvers of church altars.   After raising a family in North Dakota, Nils moved to Saskatchewan where he died in 1919.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About BARBRO NILSEDATTER LILLEGARD:
2 CONT Census: 1865, Municipality: Nes / Domicile: Rødningen Grønskalet
2 CONT Emigration: 28 Apr 1876, Departed Oslo for Albert Lea, Minnesota
