1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The youngest daughter, Gunhild, married Ole Knudsen Oyen of Nes in Hallingdal.  They had no children while they lived in Norway.  In 1857 they came to America on the sailing ship Emerald. It took six weeks to cross the ocean and t
2 CONC hey came on to Stoughton, Wisconsin.  There their first son, Knut, was born.  Ole built an oxcart and with it they moved to Goodhue County, Minnesota.  There they had four more children. In 1867 Ole died.  A few years later Gunhil
2 CONC d married Ole's Brother, Halvor Knutson.  After another few years, in 1875, Gunhild died after being kicked by a horse.  All of the Knutson children remained at Goodhue.
