1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Clara Bakke, 94, died Monday, December 21, 1998 at the CNC unit of Northwest Medical Center in Thief River Falls.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at 11 a.m. on Saturday, December 26 at Bethania Free Lutheran Church, rural Newfolden, with Reverend LeRoy Flickinger and Irvin Schmitke officiating. Kelly Liedberg was the organist. Beth Nelson was the 
2 CONC soloist, and a duet was presented by Eunice and Jared Liedberg. Casketbearers were Dwight Tangquist, Rodney Liedberg, Melville Bakken, Irvin Schmitke, James Engelsrud and John Hanson. Honorary casketbearers were all of her grandch
2 CONC ildren. Burial was in Bethania Lutheran Cemetery. The Green Funeral Home was in charge of the arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clara Marie Engelsrud was born March 31, 1904 in Marsh Grove township of Marshall county, the daughter of Christian and Caroline (Lodoen) Engelsrud. She was baptized, confirmed and attended school in Marshall county.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 18, 1929 she was united in marriage to Bertil Bakke at Newfolden. The couple lived and farmed in Marsh Grove township, rural Newfolden. In January of 1945 they moved into Newfolden, and in 1963 they moved to Thief Rive
2 CONC r Falls. Bertil died on June 26, 1983. On August 9, 1991 Clara moved to the CNC unit of Northwest Medical Center in Thief River Falls where she has since resided.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a life-long member of Bethania Free Lutheran Church and served as the church organist from 1922 until 1929. She enjoyed tatting and spending time with her children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clara is survived by three daughters, Janette (Douglas) Weber of Newfolden, and Betty (Clarence) Amiot and Vernice Nelson, both of Thief River Falls; one son, Dennis (Joanie) Bakke of Thief River Falls; 17 grandchildren; many grea
2 CONC t-grandchildren; one sister-in-law; and one niece.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, Bertil; her parents; one son-in-law, Leo Nelson; one great-grandson, Joshua Nelson; and one brother, Conrad C. Engelsrud. http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=33168815
